{"name":"Crimson Warrior","hex":"#b35138","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crimson","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, slightly bluish red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a deep red colour.","Immodest. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crimson"},{"term":"warrior","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is actively engaged in battle, conflict or warfare; a soldier or combatant.","A person who is aggressively, courageously, or energetically involved in an activity, such as athletics."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warrior"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crimson","blocks":[{"text":"Crimson is a rich, deep red color, inclining to purple. It originally meant the color of the kermes dye produced from a scale insect, Kermes vermilio, but the name is now sometimes also used as a generic term for slightly bluish-red colors that are between red and rose. It is the national color of Nepal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg/330px-Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson"},{"title":"Warrior","blocks":[{"text":"A warrior is a guardian specializing in combat or warfare, especially within the context of a tribal or clan-based warrior culture society that recognizes a separate warrior aristocracy, class, or caste."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warrior"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg/500px-Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg/500px-Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip